# Document reading typography

All document-like reading surfaces (document view/preview, Help body, Templates type detail) share **one** typography system:

- CSS: `apps/frontend/src/pages/DocumentContent.css` (class `.document-content`)
- Block preview: `DocumentBlocksPreview` (preferred when content is or can be a `BlockDocument`)
- Static pages (Help): wrap with `DocumentReadingSurface` and use `Title` / `Text component="p"` / `List` like the preview

## Do not

- Add parallel reading CSS (e.g. `.content-reading`) or page-local heading scales
- Style Help/Templates body with ad-hoc `size`/`c="dimmed"` that fights `.document-content`
- Invent a second max-width or font stack for “docs-like” columns outside `document-page-scroll` + `.document-content`

## Do

- Put new reader typography changes only in `DocumentContent.css` (and editor mirror if required)
- Prefer synthesizing a `BlockDocument` + `DocumentBlocksPreview` when showing template/outline-like content
- Reading font (sans Open Sans / serif Georgia) is user preference `documentReadingFont`; apply via
  `--document-font-family` and `document.documentElement[data-document-reading-font]` – do not hardcode
  a second stack on Help/Templates/document pages
